                        ],
                        "form": "zlewiska"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c77e7396-42a0-38e3-81d5-994bffd7b254",
                        "entry_id": "86a12325-26be-37f3-ad2b-62ce0236db56",
                        "glosses": [
                            "obszar, z jakiego wody spływają do jednego dużego zbiornika naturalnego"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "81f4c240-bcdc-47c8-9e48-c40e03d33910",
                                "sense_id": "c77e7396-42a0-38e3-81d5-994bffd7b254",
                                "text": "Sieć rzeczna jest dobrze rozwinięta, a główne rzeki to Dniestr z dopływami: Reut, Ikiel, Botna i Byk oraz Prut, należące do zlewiska Morza Czarnego."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5c6bf901-ae68-4b03-8dbe-464f0a8a5255",
                        "source_entry_id": "86a12325-26be-37f3-ad2b-62ce0236db56",
                        "source_sense_id": "c77e7396-42a0-38e3-81d5-994bffd7b254",
                        "target_lang_word": "basin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "basin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac202af0-5969-3167-8987-d557f5b147de",
                                        "entry_id": "2bc3d63d-56d1-3db4-8632-612859b364fb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A wide bowl for washing, sometimes affixed to a wall."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e2c8b8d-7628-401a-9536-f98113f46aa7",
                                                "sense_id": "ac202af0-5969-3167-8987-d557f5b147de",
                                                "text": "First, as you know, my house within the city\nIs richly furnished with plate and gold,\nBasins and ewers to lave her dainty hands;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8de9d25-2165-44c1-b6bc-dc2b2b87e8eb",
                                                "sense_id": "ac202af0-5969-3167-8987-d557f5b147de",
                                                "text": "After that he poureth water into a bason, and began to wash the disciples’ feet, and to wipe them with the towel wherewith he was girded."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f2592c2-0d61-4156-8eb3-b5744d79cdca",
                                                "sense_id": "ac202af0-5969-3167-8987-d557f5b147de",
                                                "text": "What then, you will say, must a man sit with his chops and fingers up to the ears and knuckles in grease? No; let those who cannot eat without defiling themselves, step into another room, provided with basons and towels: but I think it would be better to institute schools, where youth may learn to eat their victuals, without daubing themselves, or giving offence to the eyes of one another."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f52b33a-3523-46ab-b426-152881460a29",
                                                "sense_id": "ac202af0-5969-3167-8987-d557f5b147de",
                                                "text": "Everybody had washed before going to bed, apparently, and the bowls were ringed with a dark sediment which the hard, alkaline water had not dissolved. Shutting the door on this disorder, he turned back to the kitchen, took Mahailey’s tin basin, doused his face and head in cold water, and began to plaster down his wet hair."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa9fe3cc-e5f1-3f63-b882-c8f8e9a6d385",
                                        "entry_id": "2bc3d63d-56d1-3db4-8632-612859b364fb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A shallow bowl used for a single serving of a drink or liquidy food."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a30fea4f-ec10-4acd-a69c-7e5da3a592a4",
                                                "sense_id": "fa9fe3cc-e5f1-3f63-b882-c8f8e9a6d385",
                                                "text": "[…] Mr. John Knightley, ashamed of his ill-humour, was now all kindness and attention; and so particularly solicitous for the comfort of her father, as to seem—if not quite ready to join him in a basin of gruel—perfectly sensible of its being exceedingly wholesome […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfbe5bc8-e3bc-4ab8-b2a0-401d7037e8c3",
                                                "sense_id": "fa9fe3cc-e5f1-3f63-b882-c8f8e9a6d385",
                                                "text": "They have a good basin of coffee or cocoa for breakfast […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "518df9ff-abea-46e6-9bb3-d6b1dc632296",
                                                "sense_id": "fa9fe3cc-e5f1-3f63-b882-c8f8e9a6d385",
                                                "text": "He rose from the table; and advancing to the master, basin and spoon in hand, said: somewhat alarmed at his own temerity: ¶ ‘Please, sir, I want some more.’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c27b629-d2d7-4cc8-bb0f-5160983b0456",
                                                "sense_id": "fa9fe3cc-e5f1-3f63-b882-c8f8e9a6d385",
                                                "text": "1893, Gilbert Parker, “The March of the White Guard,” in Tavistock Tales, New York: Tait Sons & Co., p. 27,\nGaspé Toujours is drinking a basin of tea, and Jeff Hyde is fitfully dozing by the fire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2766159-8689-489c-a1f7-a9e69de16af4",
                                                "sense_id": "fa9fe3cc-e5f1-3f63-b882-c8f8e9a6d385",
                                                "text": "A steaming basin of coffee or soup revived them greatly, and even having to decide which of these refreshments they would have, and helping themselves to bread, pulled them together a little."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "30fc95f3-8f8f-3079-aa1e-fb7e025f8b72",
                                        "entry_id": "2bc3d63d-56d1-3db4-8632-612859b364fb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A depression, natural or artificial, containing water."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bae124e4-e75d-4264-8262-9bc7712e9040",
                                                "sense_id": "30fc95f3-8f8f-3079-aa1e-fb7e025f8b72",
                                                "text": "This shortly brought them to a bewitching spring, whose basin was incrusted with a frostwork of glittering crystals […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53a9bdcc-8c2d-4e63-9ac2-0d81dc4387f6",
                                                "sense_id": "30fc95f3-8f8f-3079-aa1e-fb7e025f8b72",
                                                "text": "The fountains were plashing musically into marble and alabaster basins."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90affa2c-ebcd-465c-83b9-fd0ed218c953",
                                                "sense_id": "30fc95f3-8f8f-3079-aa1e-fb7e025f8b72",
                                                "text": "There was a stone basin of clear but motionless water, and the heavy reddish-and-yellow arches went round the courtyard with warrior-like fatality, their bases in dark shadow."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc1eee5d-7047-3939-995d-4f63ede17754",
                                        "entry_id": "2bc3d63d-56d1-3db4-8632-612859b364fb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An area of land from which water drains into a common outlet; drainage basin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba8e5121-3f14-4e1c-93b9-726f2b98af2f",
                                                "sense_id": "cc1eee5d-7047-3939-995d-4f63ede17754",
                                                "text": "Devils Lake is where I began my career as a limnologist in 1964, studying the lake’s neotenic salamanders and chironomids, or midge flies. […] The Devils Lake Basin is an endorheic, or closed, basin covering about 9,800 square kilometers in northeastern North Dakota."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe0e0b67-f4ee-3d35-8001-ca4a669399ef",
                                        "entry_id": "2bc3d63d-56d1-3db4-8632-612859b364fb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A shallow depression in a rock formation, such as an area of down-folded rock that has accumulated a thick layer of sediments, or an area scooped out by water erosion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "basin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c89f5ed2-3f39-3478-9af4-05cbee5e10d4",
                                        "entry_id": "f257f027-4ccb-3a84-9f8f-b7a7df76ecbd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To create a concavity or depression in."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88ab7135-f432-4c8f-aad5-0f2e7f5dd87b",
                                                "sense_id": "c89f5ed2-3f39-3478-9af4-05cbee5e10d4",
                                                "text": "Then axial subsidence basined the surface of the dome."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed2d3493-a846-48d9-96ff-4688b4249dc5",
                                                "sense_id": "c89f5ed2-3f39-3478-9af4-05cbee5e10d4",
                                                "text": "Basining is the process that gives the faces of the dies their radius, or concavity. Depending on the production method, the planchet metal flows either toward or away from the center of the dies. The minting facilities \"basined\" the dies after they were delivered from the Philadelphia Mint's Engraving Department."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74e92f76-a4f0-4119-879e-b4508b4290e6",
                                                "sense_id": "c89f5ed2-3f39-3478-9af4-05cbee5e10d4",
                                                "text": "Of course, this is exactly what did happen—the antiquated practice of basining the dies was cast aside for the Lincoln Cent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7b25aec-1ce0-4f15-b2f3-7312a473300a",
                                                "sense_id": "c89f5ed2-3f39-3478-9af4-05cbee5e10d4",
                                                "text": "Scandinavia was basined under the load of the last or so-called Würm ice-cap."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0d66985e-38ca-38dc-9d6c-0e817c260226",
                                        "entry_id": "f257f027-4ccb-3a84-9f8f-b7a7df76ecbd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To serve as or become a basin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f33f691f-2742-4f2f-9b8c-0dd7d4900075",
                                                "sense_id": "0d66985e-38ca-38dc-9d6c-0e817c260226",
                                                "text": "To what degree this stress field formed in response to eastward movement of the African plate, to northward movement of the African plate relative to Europe, to basinning of the shelf between the eastern Canaries and Africa, or to other causes is as yet unknown."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "947d4f76-064b-463f-be24-8090e0967bc6",
                                                "sense_id": "0d66985e-38ca-38dc-9d6c-0e817c260226",
                                                "text": "The eastward pinching and thinning were caused by the rapid basining of the plateau over the Pasco-Richland area in south-central Washington."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e954d977-7858-4449-9c24-240c0e67c066",
                                                "sense_id": "0d66985e-38ca-38dc-9d6c-0e817c260226",
                                                "text": "Walls basined at a ca. 45° angle on the southwest side, but on the west and north there was little basining, with the floor sloping gently up to the original ground surface."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de493df3-f47f-4c3a-bf39-ce216856a4f6",
                                                "sense_id": "0d66985e-38ca-38dc-9d6c-0e817c260226",
                                                "text": "Deformation of the rocks involved in anticline formation increased as deformation of the rocks involved in basining decreased, and the less intense structures of the norfold facies developed in both regions."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c527c56-c03c-3782-9711-d3e91d63bcd1",
                                        "entry_id": "f257f027-4ccb-3a84-9f8f-b7a7df76ecbd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To shelter or enclose in a basin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e32c6e2d-752f-4721-b746-b9eac91a2623",
                                                "sense_id": "0c527c56-c03c-3782-9711-d3e91d63bcd1",
                                                "text": "A moan as of distant wind or thunder portended something at hand, the approach of which, basinned as we were among high broken ridges, patchy-scrubbed heights, and penned in by a maze of steep-sided gullies or gorges — we had no chance of observing, until it cam down in hurricane strength."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9db1a78-fb41-48f8-8d80-2b2fec1a3df8",
                                                "sense_id": "0c527c56-c03c-3782-9711-d3e91d63bcd1",
                                                "text": "A row of trees was basined in the latter part of April, and by the latter part of July, a little over three months, there was a remarkable improvement in the appearance of the basined row compared with the check trees."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b5bd886-3290-4e47-868c-b156f7826254",
                                                "sense_id": "0c527c56-c03c-3782-9711-d3e91d63bcd1",
                                                "text": "Caesar's subjects bathed in Caesar's blood basinned in the purple pool of Calpurnia's dream; my sister slept in an ogre's thought and woke up on the hook of a cannibal finger."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d58e29ba-7934-433a-a305-a1167cc11ba4",
                                                "sense_id": "0c527c56-c03c-3782-9711-d3e91d63bcd1",
                                                "text": "They took a narrow path through the snow, up the hill which basined the village, and on to a plateau, a stretch of sparsely treed land."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "054ccac3-acb7-4a9d-861a-13dc5eda1384",
                                                "sense_id": "0c527c56-c03c-3782-9711-d3e91d63bcd1",
                                                "text": "Well back under this natural shelter, basined in the hollowed rock, a blessed pool of fair water lay unwrinkled by even a flutter of breeze."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d78d9f35-4d97-47d9-b3b3-79c44feb4883",
                        "source_entry_id": "86a12325-26be-37f3-ad2b-62ce0236db56",
                        "source_sense_id": "c77e7396-42a0-38e3-81d5-994bffd7b254",
                        "target_lang_word": "catchment",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "catchment",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "909124af-650b-3553-81c8-8dbcdd4ace72",
                                        "entry_id": "71440f61-2c01-3e8d-ad52-d80dbde8dc83",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any structure or land feature which catches and holds water; the collection of such water."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "attributive",
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81835eff-160e-409c-8174-77d9a097ecce",
                                                "sense_id": "909124af-650b-3553-81c8-8dbcdd4ace72",
                                                "text": "Do you think that there ought to be some board or some authority for each catchment basin, which must be appointed with adequate powers to prevent the pollution of streams?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2020c43-2e60-4491-a687-9b0e6976e2d4",
                                                "sense_id": "909124af-650b-3553-81c8-8dbcdd4ace72",
                                                "text": "[paragraph 515] Now let us come to this point: you are quite clear that serious evil exists in this union of navigation and drainage? […] [paragraph 517] And you are also clear that one obstacle is the taxation of the catchment area, and that it needs some plan to be devised for meeting it, although this plan may have defects?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea458423-437e-4aed-97be-26562646a95e",
                                                "sense_id": "909124af-650b-3553-81c8-8dbcdd4ace72",
                                                "text": "The catchment area is the slope of a great mountain range covered with fine forests, and there are many good reservoir sites."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e53637de-15cf-4c1e-8703-c1c31603cb93",
                                                "sense_id": "909124af-650b-3553-81c8-8dbcdd4ace72",
                                                "text": "Isotope hydrograph separations determined by simple conservative-mixing models have shown repeatedly, in a variety of climactic and hydrogeologic environments, that streamflow generated during rainfall or snowmelt is derived primarily from water stored in the catchment prior to the event, a surprising insight that has profoundly changed how hydrologists view the runoff process. […] Catchment hydrology is more than just the study of water, or rocks, or biota – it encompasses the physical and biogeochemical interactions that control the hydrology and biogeochemistry of the system."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d11926b-f1d1-48d8-b32f-30a3159e74d0",
                                                "sense_id": "909124af-650b-3553-81c8-8dbcdd4ace72",
                                                "text": "Every mountain in Petra has carved water channels in the indigenous stone that catch the seasonal erosion floods. Every building seems to be positioned to maximize water catchment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb0b8a9d-a95c-3df1-9082-6e112df8583f",
                                        "entry_id": "71440f61-2c01-3e8d-ad52-d80dbde8dc83",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A catchment area, or the people it serves."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd159bf9-55f6-47be-8acd-d6f675a90a3a",
                                                "sense_id": "cb0b8a9d-a95c-3df1-9082-6e112df8583f",
                                                "text": "The Hospital Plan first set out the objective: a network of large district general hospitals, each providing specialised medical and surgical facilities for a catchment of 200,000 to 300,000 population[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a8c3737-583a-42ca-b886-1fd39198c977",
                                                "sense_id": "cb0b8a9d-a95c-3df1-9082-6e112df8583f",
                                                "text": "The publication of regular newsletters providing updates of floodplain management activities and distributed to individual residents in the catchment is an effective means of keeping the community informed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc85ee7c-c1b9-41e0-85e8-d00bcf6eec21",
                                                "sense_id": "cb0b8a9d-a95c-3df1-9082-6e112df8583f",
                                                "text": "In August 2019, Redcar & Cleveland and Middlesbrough councils announced details of a joint project, supported by TVCA to build a new park and ride station on the Whitby line between Nunthorpe and Great Ayton. The two councils say the station would have a population catchment of 70,000 from local towns and villages."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "catchment",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8b843340-ae0a-3d9a-9e6a-24cc015f6726",
                                        "entry_id": "fee59c7b-b22d-301e-9826-786cc9c8b47c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To divide into catchment areas."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "032b46c7-415d-4b0f-a323-26cefec63428",
                                                "sense_id": "8b843340-ae0a-3d9a-9e6a-24cc015f6726",
                                                "text": "the catchmenting of mental health services"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "404104ae-6b7d-469c-9ae9-b5c1eff32b1f",
                        "source_entry_id": "86a12325-26be-37f3-ad2b-62ce0236db56",
